{title: These Hands}
{artist: Jeff Deyo}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]The sun and moon[D], and every star[C], are there to show [D]me who You are[C],
I can be [D]sure Your [Am]fingerprints are [C]everywhere.
[C]My every move[D], my every [C]breath, were meant to [D]point to Your [C]greatness,
There's nothing [D]made that was not [Am]made to show Your [D]power.

{comment: Chorus}
[G]These hands, were made [D]to praise You,
[Em]These lips, were made [C]to lift You up[G],
[G]I give, to [D]You my life, in [Am]worship[B].  [C]

[G]These feet, were [D]made to serve You
[Em]This tongue, to [C]sing of Your [G]great love.
[G]I give, to [D]You my life, in [Am]worship[B].   [C]

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]A tender [D]thought, a caring deed[C], a gift of love [D]to one in need[C],
Bringing [D]honest acts of [Am]worship to You [B]Lord.

{comment: Bridge 1}
[Am]Lifting holy [C]hands in [G]worship to [B]You, [D]Lord.
[Am]God [C]receive this humble [G]sacrifice, of [E]praise.

{comment: Bridge 2}
[C]I give to You my [Am]life, [C]my life to you in [Am]worship  [C]
In worship[D],   [C]In worship[D]
[C]My life, [D]I give [C]in [G]worship
